   "inflation": "Inflation remains elevated. Today's policy action will support a timelier return to the Committee's 2 percent goal."
  },
  "press_conference_quotes": [
   {
    "quote": "This summer's inflation readings do not tell me that underlying trends have meaningfully improved.",
    "speaker": "Chair Kevin Warsh",
    "context": "on why the Fed hiked despite growth resilience"
   },
   {
    "quote": "We cannot affect any individual price, but what we can do and will do is ensure that any change in relative prices don't broaden out, don't have second and third order effects on the economy.",
    "speaker": "Chair Kevin Warsh",
    "context": "citing oil and groceries as examples of relative-price moves the Fed will not chase, but guarding against broadening"
   },
   {
    "quote": "I would say these things tend to be overdetermined. This is a complicated set of things that are affecting the most important asset anywhere in the world, the 10-year Treasury.",
    "speaker": "Chair Kevin Warsh",
    "context": "on drivers of the 10-year Treasury yield"
   },
   {
    "quote": "Those who are least well off have the most to gain from a durable expansion, a solid labor market, and stable prices.",
